{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/435111-house-ruled-2-0-bale-hounds","id":435111,"title":"House ruled 2.0 Bale Hounds","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-09T19:25:25-07:00","id":435111,"title":"House ruled 2.0 Bale Hounds","content":"Bale Hounds ~ <i>Asah Gadar</i> (Note, this write up assumes them as a secret 9th tribe from the Blasphemies book)<br /> <br /> Sacred Prey: None. The Bale Hounds activities do not leave them with time to hunt. Attending a Siskur Dah is rare at best, and as such they more often then not miss out. The consequences of this can be abated by a ritual taught by their First Born totem, Soulless Wolf. <br /> <br /> Rite of the Sin Eater (can be renamed, I'm just converting it as best as my amateur self can) **<br /> Symbols: Blood, Betrayal, maeljin sins, silver blade.<br /> The only symbol truly required is the silver blade. The Asah Gadar may only perform this rite in a wound, with out without the presence of Soulless Wolf. The rite master can only perform the rite upon himself, and must spend at least two essence to initiate the rite, as well as provide an offering to his dark lords (trophies from his activities or something symbolizing the sins of the maeljin ideals). Common materials for the rite include the remains of individuals who exemplified the particular sin in their mortal lives (a gambler for greed, etc...) The Asah Gadar pleads for the pleasures the sacred hunt brings, listing his activities to his lords as proof of his worthiness for the boon (or abatement of consequences from not hunting). The supplicant cuts himself deep enough to bleed for a full 9 minutes, dealing two points of lethal damage to himself and spends at least 2 essence while once again beseeching his lords for their aid. The dice roll comes after the lengthy ritual (as per first edition rules).<br /> <br /> Dice pool: Same as Siskur Dah. For each point of essence spent above the initial 2, add an additional bonus to the roll.<br /> <br /> Dramatic Failure: The rite is failed and the hound must wait a full month to try again. <br /> <br /> Failure: the rite fails but may be retried so long as the Hound has the necessary materials.<br /> <br /> Success: Soulless wolf appears before the supplicant ad consumes the offering and bale hounds blood. For the next month the hound feels as though they have performed Siskur Dah. For Hounds with higher primal urge they may need to perform this ritual multiple times per month. <br /> <br /> Exceptional success: The hound receives the benefits to the extent that she will not feel the need to hunt for 3 lunar months.<br /> <br /> <br /> In this way the Asah Gadar may operate as his Forsaken or Pure counter parts, without the obvious problems from ignoring the call to the hunt.<br /> <br /> <br /> Feel free to add to or change this in any way. Just thought I'd take a stab at updating them and keeping what I felt to be their signature ritual intact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T20:20:54-07:00","id":435195,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't say they don't have time to hunt. They hunt whatever the packs they're infiltrating hunt. They wouldn't exactly fit in as infiltrators if they didn't hunt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T20:33:06-07:00","id":435207,"title":"","content":"Fair enough. I was thinking of a way to include the sin eater ritual in a way that added similar benefits as it did in 1e. That jumped to what benefits does the siskur dah grant and boom. I'd hate to see the ritual wasted as it was one of their major tethers to Soulless Wolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}